# Probability Theory

Probability theory is the branch of mathematics concerned with probability. 
It provides the mathematical framework for modeling uncertainty and randomness.

## Core Concepts

A central concept in this field is the [Random Variable](random_variable.dj), which maps outcomes of a random phenomenon to numbers. 

When dealing with systems that evolve over time under probabilistic rules, we study a [Stochastic Process](stochastic_process.dj).

## Applications

- Statistical mechanics
- Machine learning
- Financial mathematics